    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` field on the owner response. When more than 80 owners have already been created for the current business day, the field is `true`; otherwise `false`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only boolean `bulkSignupWarning` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (and getter/setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"bulkSignupWarning\", ignore = true)` on `toOwnerDto`, since it's a controller-computed value not present on the `Owner` model.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added the `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and an `isBulkSignupDay()` helper that reuses the existing daily-accumulation path \u2014 `countOwnersRegisteredOn(toBusinessDay(LocalDate.now())) > 80`.\n   - Set `ownerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(isBulkSignupDay())` on both the `addOwner` (create) and `getOwner` responses.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` (asserting the `false` branch via `GET /api/owners/{id}`) passes, along with the full suite (261 tests green). The `>80` branch is driven by the same accumulation path the existing daily-limit rule uses, consistent with the test's note.",
